{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1157439-how-complicated-should-infernals-be","id":1157439,"title":"How complicated should Infernals be?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Infernal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-11-09T20:55:39-08:00","id":1157439,"title":"How complicated should Infernals be?","content":"So, I'm all for the idea of moving to Ability Charms for Green Sun Princes, and everything that might mean for them being more mechanically and thematically solid. But I do have certain concerns when the subject of yet another Yozi that their powers can be based off of comes up.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt's mostly a case of the worry that they could go off in too many directions at once, or become overburdened, particularly in contrast to their counterparts. The cohesion of Solars is fairly self-evident, but I find the comparison to Abyssals to be particularly of note.<br /> <br /> \u200bI don't have the same concern with Abyssals because the figures that would serve as inspiration for their powers, the Deathlords, are not too far off from what the deathknights themselves are. They may be a different order of being, but aesthetically they're still human shaped things engaging in various kinds of human activities (if bad ones) with deathly powers that can generally be expected to extend from their human imagery. That and there aren't too many of them, and there's a clear aesthetic and thematic thoroughline between all of them. I presume that in the end, you could present Abyssals to somebody who knew nothing about the Deathlords, and they would hold together and make sense; the First and Forsaken Lion and Lover Clad in Raiment of Tears might help one <i>write</i> respective Resistance and Presence Charms, but I don't think they're necessary in order to read them, or make sense of both of those things coming from the same group.<br /> <br /> \u200bAs inspirations for the powers of Exalted, the Yozis are stranger and more varied, and that raises a few concerns for me. One is that it could be harder to come up with Charms inspired by certain Yozis that would not lean too much into them; that whether you call it an Athletics Charm or not, if you reference Isidoros too heavily in it, it still ultimately comes across as an Isidoros Charm by another name. I would fear if that might create a lack of cohesion between any such Charms and anything else in Athletics. A kind of worry that somebody couldn't really make sense of the Charms if they didn't know the Yozis.<br /> <br /> \u200bConversely, I would have a worry that if the Yozis don't get referenced heavily, you would wind up with something that seems like a random grab bag.<br /> <br /> \u200bAs another contrast to Abyssals, it's like... when I saw the published Solar Presence Charms and how they mirrored the provisional Abyssal ones, it put the Abyssals in proper perspective for me. It gave me a sense that, as an inversion of Solars, there's a clear, core sense of what an Abyssal is, and for them Deathlord inspiration becomes a matter of dressing that up and giving it direction, rather than building Abyssals entirely out of Deathlord associations.<br /> <br /> \u200bWith Infernals, I would wonder if there's a sense of an essential Hellish Solar where any given Yozi might be considered a matchup to something that a Solar might do and provides a similar thing to what the Deathlords do with Abyssals, or is the intention and permission of Yozi inspirations that Infernal Abilities go off in all kinds of wild directions?<br /> <br /> \u200bI hope that I don't come across as arguing for Green Solars. I'm just trying to establish a sense of how far Yozis as inspirations for their powers goes, and communicate some worries that creates about their cohesion.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-09T21:18:54-08:00","id":1157447,"title":"","content":"I favor/prefer broken, incoherent, grab bag effects in the Infernal Charmset. By the time of the Infernals in an edition's run, it needs shaken up, and a little madness does the trick. Reflecting broken, jarred beings in this meta way is, for me, a feature, not a bug. Also I'm a sucker for transhumanism, which may color my opinion. <br /> <br /> I get your point about having to read the Yozis to understand the Charms, but I have faith that the writers can loop it the other way around - by reading the Infernals Charmset, you <i>come to know </i>the Yozis. To grognards like you and me, not having read every word about the Yozis feels like an incomplete picture - but to someone who has only read rocking Isidoros Athletics Charms, he's the heavy metal bull who's the model for your hell powers, and that should make him cool enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-09T21:21:28-08:00","id":1157449,"title":"","content":"Okay, third tries the charm.<br /> I think there are, as you suggest, 2 ways to approch this problem.<br /> 1: What connects the 15 yozi asethetically?<br /> 2: what is the centeral theme of the Infernals, seperate from the Yozi, as inversion of Solars is seperate from deathlords?<br /> <br /> 1. I feel like there must be based on feeling. By which I mean, when reading homebrew Yozis, I get a feeling occasionally that this or that feels off or like it doesn't belong. I've said elsewhere I have suspcions of what could be a good link (for exaltation) between Yozi and Infernal, but thats not between the Yozi themselves. For that, I might go to some fact that they are singluar and absolute reference points, even among themselves? Like, all their descriptors feel like they need a THE. Which, for a group of 15 odd named individuals, makes sense. But beyond that and to what aesthetic, I'd have to spend a lot of time thinking and looking over Games of Divinity. Maybe something about their basic inhumanity? But that's not a good thing to build on. Hm...Anyway.<br /> 2.THis one I have a few better stabs at. So, one thing that was mentioned in the ask devs that might be intreasting here is the existence of &quot;normal&quot; infernal charms that cover things like Budding PYsche bits into demons or making personal otherworlds. And that gives a tip as to infernal themes/concept/etc of hellish solars. Infernals are self-altering and self defining. Their a version of solars that has left Plato's Gold Philospher king (heh) to become Nietzche's ubermensch. I want a non-Nietzche reference for that, but that seems to align with the infernals and the Yozi to a degree. Hell, it works iwth the idea of each Infernal having their own Shintai, molding their body into a divine vessel/true expression of themeselves.<br /> <br /> ...which even if true is a terribly hard thing to balance, cuz Infernals self definition needs some coherence to it, other wise it's the &quot;make up what you wanna be&quot; tree. So probably,answering one will lead into answering 2? I'm thinking of the preivewed charms, and trying to think of how the &quot;eating memories&quot; adjoran stealth charms are meanignfully reflective of the identiy of Infenrals vs Solars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-09T22:07:33-08:00","id":1157458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tikor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1157439-how-complicated-should-infernals-be?p=1157447#post1157447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">by reading the Infernals Charmset, you <i>come to know </i>the Yozis.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI don't care about the Yozis; I want to know about the Infernals.<br /> <br /> \u200bI think that's really at the heart of my concern; there gets to be a point where people expressing excitement about all the possibilities of Charms inspired by <i>even more</i> Yozis becomes all about the giant monsters locked outside of the world forever, and the Exalted become window dressing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, one thing that was mentioned in the ask devs that might be intreasting here is the existence of &quot;normal&quot; infernal charms that cover things like Budding PYsche bits into demons or making personal otherworlds.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bOther worlds is still something that I have reservations about, but I have sometimes thought about the image of creating and implanting miniature demons as a way of expressing certain effects.<br /> <br /> \u200bBut where the demon involved is just a means to an end, rather than the point of the exercise; like a Sidereal Charm creating a personal pattern spider to retrieve information for you.<br /> <br /> \u200bOtherwise, I often find demon creation to be something that has an issue with not exactly having many places to go.<br /> <br /> \u200bPlus the concern about making something pivotal to characters that necessarily requires a lot of homebrew or improvisation.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T02:40:16-08:00","id":1157486,"title":"","content":"Folding the stuff everyone liked from Broken Winged Crane into the core Infernal experience sounds like a good idea, as long as you're careful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T03:01:45-08:00","id":1157487,"title":"","content":"I suppose it won't hurt to talk about this now.<br /> <br /> John once talked to me about plans for 3e Infernals and at the time envisioned a mechanic that seemed reminiscent of the Bridge keyword but for charms that drew upon the thematics of a specific Yozi so there was an advantage to jumping off of (for example) Melee to follow Malfeas thematically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T04:57:19-08:00","id":1157497,"title":"","content":"When I try to resolve the question, I keep trying to think of what the core image of Infernals ought to be.<br /> <br /> \u200bNow for me, that is... well, Maleficent. Or, as something more transmissible to a variety of character concepts, terrible sorcerer kings of old.<br /> <br /> \u200bWhen I think about that, I have a clearer idea on how powers inspired by the Yozis can come together as a coherent whole; you don't focus on the Yozis, you mine them for things to represent the capabilities of the dread witch kings. Elloge is a valid source of inspiration, but don't tell me about her, don't even mention her, just tell me about freaky Linguistics Charms that, just off the top of my head, has the arguments of the Green Sun Prince extend from their mouth as tendrils of words that wrap themselves around another and physically bind them.<br /> <br /> I think if that was the subject of emphasis, even Linguistics Charms that manifest through a variety of effects would feel interconnected. It's an impression that I got off of those provisional Stealth Charms.<br /> <br /> Shintais are a whole other thing, and an area where I think the Yozi connection can be more apparent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T07:29:41-08:00","id":1157526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1157439-how-complicated-should-infernals-be?p=1157458#post1157458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bOther worlds is still something that I have reservations about, but I have sometimes thought about the image of creating and implanting miniature demons as a way of expressing certain effects.<br /> <br /> \u200bBut where the demon involved is just a means to an end, rather than the point of the exercise; like a Sidereal Charm creating a personal pattern spider to retrieve information for you.<br /> <br /> \u200bOtherwise, I often find demon creation to be something that has an issue with not exactly having many places to go.<br /> <br /> \u200bPlus the concern about making something pivotal to characters that necessarily requires a lot of homebrew or improvisation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant more as examples of non-Yozi(maybe?) character charms. THey say something about imposing or projecting the self outward onto the world in a way that Solars at the moment don't. I kinda think they might integrity charms (Make demons out of intimacies to supress them or to protect them) or the like. <br /> I do think the image &quot;ancient sorcerer king&quot; might work, but it feels less...clear to me then &quot;knights of death&quot; and &quot;glorious golden sun prince&quot;. But it'll probably be clearer with more charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T07:41:12-08:00","id":1157528,"title":"","content":"Solars can whip up a new god with Occult Charms. Would be strange for Infernals to not be able to do something similar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T08:15:31-08:00","id":1157539,"title":"","content":"Isator, I agree with you, and I'm a bit worried about it too. I do think the devs have mentioned a few things I feel encouraged by, but there is a fundamental issue.<br /> <br /> With Abyssals, it's quite simple to understand their themes. It's all about undead, ghosts, death, shadows, etc.<br /> <br /> When I read the Infernal book, I thought they were really cool.<br /> But when I played one, it felt very much like I had 3 different entirely-unlinked power sets in one character (green fire powers, running powers, and sand control). And I didn't feel like my character had any great link to the other 4 Infernals in his coven, they just seemed like a really random group of people with random people.<br /> <br /> Actually, the best Infernal character I saw picked 95% of her charms from Malfeas and Cecylene, and was very much a demonic-cult leader who could punch with green fire. That way the powers seemed to have some kind of thematic link. She didn't have any powers about insane running, or invisible force tentacles.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The thing is, that Abyssals are based on pretty straightforward genre-tropes. Vampire knight. Lich. Revenant. Sexy vampire. Vampire wizard. Necromancer.<br /> <br /> But Infernals aren't, because the writers of Exalted 1st ed explicitly didn't want Judeo-Christian demons as the theme. You don't have Infernals throwing hellfire and growing hooves, red scales and wings, or sacrificing virgins on pentagrams. (They did do a bit of wish-granting with Cecylene, which worked well actually).<br /> <br /> They've got bits of judeo-Christian demon mythology, bits of various eastern demon mythology, bits of Cthulu mythos, but a lot more of random mad craziness.<br /> This makes it much more difficult to build a thematically-linked Infernal charm set, where the Athletics charms and the Presence charms and the Lore charms and the Bureaucracy charms actually all feel like they're from the same thematic core, than it is for Abyssals, Solars, Lunars or even Sidereals.<br /> <br /> <br /> And I do think that, to some extent, the answer is not to lean in to the Yozis too much. Have more &quot;this is what Infernal powers are&quot;, with bits that mention the Yozis, rather than &quot;you wield 25 disparate power sets of entirely different god-monster-worlds.&quot; Not to write the Yozis out entirely, but make Infernals feel like their own thing, not exigents of the Yozis.<br /> <br /> I hope that doing Ability charms rather than Yozi charms means that what it is to be an Infernal, rather than just what it is to be a Yozi, can be explored a bit more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 11-10-2017, 11:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T08:18:03-08:00","id":1157541,"title":"","content":"I've got to say, Infernals were the only Exalt-type whose book I loved, whose rules I loved, who I was really excited to play, and then within a few sessions decided I didn't like after all. (With 2 different characters). I don't know if anyone else found that, but only one player in our group (who as I mentioned, thought his character through carefully and created a character who did work thematically) continued playing Infernals, most people tried them and then went back to DBs, Solars and Lunars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T08:22:35-08:00","id":1157543,"title":"","content":"Maybe instead of a supernal ability infernals could get a supernal Yozi?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T08:49:40-08:00","id":1157554,"title":"","content":"I really hope not. That'd just lead back to the problem I had before, which is connected to over-emphasising the Yozis' powers* within the Infernal powerset. <br /> <br /> *Actually, a charm set based around a single Yozi would work fine in terms of the problem of theme, it's just that there probably isn't enough there for a whole PC charmset. The problem is emphasising 5(+) entirely different Yozis.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> You know, weirdly, I wouldn't really mind so much if the Infernal actually learned the Yozi's powers from the Yozi. Or learned demonic-themed powers from demons. That'd make it feel more like they'd learnt a disparate group of esoteric and magical techniques for power. But that's probably also impractical from a splat-book perspective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T08:53:07-08:00","id":1157555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1157439-how-complicated-should-infernals-be?p=1157543#post1157543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe instead of a supernal ability infernals could get a supernal Yozi?</div> </div> </div> </div>If each abillity had 1 yozi to it (Malfeas does Resistance, Qaf Integrity, Cecylne does...Survival?), that might work.<br /> My big problem with infernals was that, well, it felt hard to do visual thematics that were distinct from the really specific Yozi thematics. Like, if my Cecylne focused character lives in a jungle, sandstrike powers seem weird.<br /> And Ceylne gives a good problem with 1 abillity 1 Yozi caveat I mentioned. Cecylene should have survial charms...but probably also, given her nature as judge, Bueracracy charms. Malfeas should be resistance, but also presence. But not all presence, because wow, I can't imagine Cecylene's cult leader idea without presence. And so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T08:53:07-08:00","id":1157556,"title":"","content":"Douuuuble poooost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T09:05:57-08:00","id":1157560,"title":"","content":"I'm not terribly worried about this honestly.<br /> <br /> I look at it from the perspective of crafting a charmset. Take athletics for example. Right now we have the solar charmset with its seemingly random assortment of completely different effects. You've got balance charms in there, jumping charms, running charms, and your strength charms. You've got Herculean strength, the flash and Wuxia running and fighting in the same ability! All of these are the base charms of separate ideas within athletics that are combined further up the tree. Strength and jumping combine into a death-from-above style attack, balance and speed combine into running across water and then running up walls and ceilings etc.<br /> <br /> For infernals this might look more like: Breaking things with the implacability of Isodorous, Running with the speed of Adorjan, combining into flying, or running through objects without stopping (&quot;I'm the Juggernaut, Bitch!&quot;), or something completely different. Perhaps we'll get a shintai of turning into a raging tornado, sucking everything in and destroying it. Perhaps in the war tree you'll take the themes of being in charge from Malfeas and the hierarchy of SWLiHN, and the rules of Cecelyne into a a fighting force that reacts to your will instantly and with perfect cohesion.<br /> <br /> Just because you're starting with different ideas doesn't mean you can't combine those into new and amazing things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":8804,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","user":"armyofwhispers","date":". 11-10-2017, 12:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T09:22:29-08:00","id":1157566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1157439-how-complicated-should-infernals-be?p=1157560#post1157560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right now we have the solar charmset with its seemingly random assortment of completely different effects. You've got balance charms in there, jumping charms, running charms, and your strength charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>How is that random?<br /> <br /> \u200bI actually think you make a good point about lines of Yozi inspiration for a logically cohesive Ability (although it touches on opposite concerns where any kind of Yozi reference might be perfunctory to what is otherwise an unmodified Solar Charm cascade), but come on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T09:35:46-08:00","id":1157574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1157439-how-complicated-should-infernals-be?p=1157566#post1157566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How is that random?<br /> <br /> \u200bI actually think you make a good point about lines of Yozi inspiration for a logically cohesive Ability (although it touches on opposite concerns where any kind of Yozi reference might be perfunctory to what is otherwise an unmodified Solar Charm cascade), but come on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps random isn't the right word there. Disparate? Unconnected? Dissimilar? <br /> <br /> What I mean is that you've got charms emulating things out of multiple different genres in the same charmset that then build into other, completely different things that then build into uniquely exalted thing.<br /> <br /> Like I said, you've got Hercules, The Flash, and Crouching Tiger, Hidden Dragon all in the same ability. These aren't a random assortment, but they sure don't go together normally. Only in Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T13:35:10-08:00","id":1157625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1157439-how-complicated-should-infernals-be?p=1157574#post1157574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Like I said, you've got Hercules, The Flash, and Crouching Tiger, Hidden Dragon all in the same ability. These aren't a random assortment, but they sure don't go together normally. Only in Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>What, super strength, speed and dexterity?<br /> <br /> \u200bThat's every Flying Brick ever.<br /> <br /> \u200bHeracles also has at least one legend where he wins a foot race against a distinctly, possibly supernatural, capable opponent, and depending on what you mean by Crouching Tiger Hidden Dragon, that's not exactly out of sorts for him either.<br /> <br /> \u200bThere's a distinct difference between drawing from a number of fictional sources to create a comprehensive picture of divine athletic capability, and some possibilities for how many directions one might follow the Yozis through that.<br /> <br /> \u200bI mean, running, jumping and lifting are dissimilar? They're close enough to go in the Olympics. And just about every all-purpose gymnasium I'm sure I could find.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T14:17:55-08:00","id":1157636,"title":"","content":"I am a bit wary about Infernals in 3rd edition, since it sounds like they will end up being more like Sidereal and Dragon Blooded. Or worse, having different Yozi-inspired Charms serve as prerequisites for one another (I want this Adorjan Charm but first I have to pick up an Ebon Dragon and a Malfeas Charm). If either of those happen, it seems like you will end up with a character who sometimes acts like the Ebon Dragon, and sometimes acts like Malfeas, and sometimes acts like Cecelyne, simply dependent on what Charm you happen to be using. In such a case you wouldn't have a character with a very strong central theme. That's always an issue for me, at least, and the reason why Dragon Blooded and Sidereal have always been my least favorite Exalted.<br /> <br /> So for Infernals I hope that within each Ability you end up with different Charm trees that draw on different Yozi. So for example within Presence you might have some a cluster of Charms inspired by Malfeas, a cluster of Charms inspired by the Ebon Dragon and a cluster of Charms inspired by Cecelyne. As a player if you wanted to, you could pick up all of those Charms, or just the ones that fit your character theme.<br /> <br /> We've already seen something like this with Solars in 3rd edition. Several Abilities have their Charms split into individual trees that focus on different aspects of that Ability. For example, in Archery you have your Wise Arrow Charm tree and your Phantom Arrow Charm tree. Just using this as a conscious base for Infernal Charms, and designing them around a similar idea, with different aspects of a given Ability would be a fair way to do it I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-12T13:57:31-08:00","id":1157988,"title":"","content":"Personally I loved infernals in 2nd edition, Fae have always been my favourites in Exalted but if picking from Exalted only my 1st edition favourites were DB\u2019s followed by Abyssals, enough so that they were the only Exalt type I played as long as the ST would agree. But then again my tumpata favourite thing with them was dice head long into a single Yozi Charm set, picking up only a few necessarily or particularly suitable Charms from the other sets. Yes it left me with certain vulnerabilities but it also gave me fun and interesting characters that really needed to manipulate the conditions so that they could excell.<br /> <br /> But then again I did love the transhumanism angle for them.<br /> <br /> So personally I hope that 3rd edition Green Sun Princes are able to go into similarly strange places as they used to, further away from the human into something else entirely. Did I mention that I am also one of the few that didn\u2019t particularly like the Devil Tiger solution in Crane? I liked the idea of being able to become something akin to what 2nd edition Primordials were and I hope 3rd edition allows them to evolve into something else as well even though it wont be an actual Yozi who, as far as I have understood, have been returned into greater concepts of 1st edition that couldn\u2019t really be pinned down with clear rules.<br /> <br /> GSP\u2019s are the Exalt\u2019s I most eagerly await, even though I am nervous of how they will end up like. The greatest change I would wish for them is their Caste marks, I already houseruled Slayer mark into a twisted spiral like Green Sun symbol, \u2019cause Ligier you know, and because I hated the crossed swords as a caste mark, similarly to the hour glass, the rest were good as they were.<br /> <br /> But again YMMV and we can ultimately only sait and see what the developers will give us in a 5-10 years it will take the line to reach Infernals if they are again the final splats given to us along the alchemicals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-12T14:22:50-08:00","id":1157993,"title":"","content":"If the splat requires intense pre-existing setting knowledge for me to engage with their themes, it's not a plus. If you can't address the themes of Infernals without quoting from lore you have lost the ability to sell Infernals to me. It does not appeal to me to know that an entire tree of charms are related to [Yozi] instead of an entire tree of charms related to an ability, which then is FLAVORED in unique directions by a or multiple Yozi's via branches off the main charm tree or cloud.<br /> <br /> When you describe the Infernals splat, if you can't describe what they do without using the word Yozi (or a bunch of other hyper specific capital-letter setting words) you have failed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Incentive is not permission or justification.","edited":{"userid":255,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","user":"ParanoiaCombo","date":". 11-12-2017, 05:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","name":"ParanoiaCombo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar255_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-12T14:35:26-08:00","id":1157995,"title":"","content":"I can see not wanting to feel obligated to get powers that don't follow the character that you have in mind, but I feel as though leaning too heavily on things that follow the capabilities or aesthetics of just one Yozi is going back to that thing of it feeling less like Infernal Exalted are a thing, and more like there being ones for each Yozi.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat's why I'm trying to think of a central concept that effects resembling a whole bunch of Yozis can live in, as well as how much the resemblance should be limited to create capabilities that don't make it feel as though a character has too many directions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-12T14:52:48-08:00","id":1157999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ParanoiaCombo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1157439-how-complicated-should-infernals-be?p=1157993#post1157993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the splat requires intense pre-existing setting knowledge for me to engage with their themes, it's not a plus. If you can't address the themes of Infernals without quoting from lore you have lost the ability to sell Infernals to me. It does not appeal to me to know that an entire tree of charms are related to [Yozi] instead of an entire tree of charms related to an ability, which then is FLAVORED in unique directions by a or multiple Yozi's via branches off the main charm tree or cloud.</div> </div> </div> </div>When it comes to that as an issue, then I would think that Sidereal are even worse off, what with how their Charms are filtered through the Maidens. You can't really look at why Sidereal Medicine is about killing people and fighting zombies unless you understand what Saturn's themes are and that Sidereal Medicine is about the Medicine Ability filtered through Saturn's themes. Plus of course things start getting especially odd when you have Charms in an Ability that don't even really have anything to do with that Ability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-12T15:00:51-08:00","id":1158001,"title":"","content":"Its possible that Sidereal Charms might undergo some kind of reworking to try to account for issues like that in Third Edition too, not unlike Infernals (though infinitely less dramatic).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-12T15:01:34-08:00","id":1158002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1157439-how-complicated-should-infernals-be?p=1157999#post1157999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When it comes to that as an issue, then I would think that Sidereal are even worse off, what with how their Charms are filtered through the Maidens. You can't really look at why Sidereal Medicine is about killing people and fighting zombies unless you understand what Saturn's themes are and that Sidereal Medicine is about the Medicine Ability filtered through Saturn's themes. Plus of course things start getting especially odd when you have Charms in an Ability that don't even really have anything to do with that Ability.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't disagree with their previous portrayals as having this problem. I don't think it's really that hard though to replace Maidens with more generalized and understandable forms of cultural understandings of things like time, destiny, etc plus they also have themes of MiB's and other deep-cover operatives. I don't like that you omitted my latter sentence to make this argument.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Incentive is not permission or justification.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","name":"ParanoiaCombo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar255_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-12T15:27:38-08:00","id":1158007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1157439-how-complicated-should-infernals-be?p=1157625#post1157625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What, super strength, speed and dexterity?<br /> <br /> \u200bThat's every Flying Brick ever.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure that superman was an inspiration for a few different parts of exalted. Parts of the athletics tree could definitely model his abilities. Well... some of them. Once again, the running over water thing is not a superman ability. That's straight up MA movies of the Wuxia genre. Or the flash. Or possibly even The Incredibles. The point is that the sources are still different. AFAIK there aren't any solar charmsets that can be traced to a single inspiration.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1157439-how-complicated-should-infernals-be?p=1157625#post1157625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bHeracles also has at least one legend where he wins a foot race against a distinctly, possibly supernatural, capable opponent, and depending on what you mean by Crouching Tiger Hidden Dragon, that's not exactly out of sorts for him either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I'm sorry, I must have missed the Greek legend where Hercules was dancing on treetops and running across water. Weird. Seems somewhat out of keeping with his normal powers.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1157439-how-complicated-should-infernals-be?p=1157625#post1157625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bThere's a distinct difference between drawing from a number of fictional sources to create a comprehensive picture of divine athletic capability, and some possibilities for how many directions one might follow the Yozis through that.</div> </div> </div> </div>You understand that the Yozi are also fictional sources right? Like there does not exist an actual city made of brass that dances really good?<br /> <br /> My point is that the solar charm trees already pull from disparate sources. Infernal charm trees are still going to pull from disparate sources. Not once did I say that the athletics charm trees weren't all associated with athletics.<br /> <br /> The solar charmset was drawn from a lot more than 15 sources. There's a lot of material there. I fail to see how the infernals are supposed to be <i>more</i> complicated than the solars.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1157439-how-complicated-should-infernals-be?p=1157625#post1157625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bI mean, running, jumping and lifting are dissimilar? They're close enough to go in the Olympics. And just about every all-purpose gymnasium I'm sure I could find.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is exactly why olympic athletes compete in all of those categories simultaneously right? Wait, no, they don't.<br /> Is your point here that all olympic sports should be modeled via athletics or something else? You do know that marksmanship, equestrianism and fencing are all olympics sports too right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-12T15:40:44-08:00","id":1158010,"title":"","content":"armyofwhispers, I think you're nitpicking and looking at the way Exalted relates to its sources of inspiration through an overly narrow lens. I find these to not make for a very useful comparison to Infernals, or analysis of Solars in general.<br /> <br /> I also think that there are some <i>very</i> different applications of terminology going on here.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat's the extent of what I can find the energy to argue for that particular line of discussion.<br /> <br /> \u200bI agree with ParanoiaCombo's point in a general sense, and especially as it regards this topic. I would consider Sidereals an exception to that, along with many other things about that particular group. I would not look to Sidereals for any kind of inspiration for the Green Sun Princes, because Sidereals are doing something <i>very</i> different in terms of who they are as people and how they act in the world. I can't think of more to say on that subject that would be on topic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-12T17:31:07-08:00","id":1158031,"title":"","content":"The Solar charmset is very tight and coherent. It's about being good at doing the stuff that you do, and shows very clear and logical progressions through intuitively assembled trees. You start with a person who is good at lifting weights and running, then add Solar charms and now have someone who's really, really, really good at lifting weights and running. There are some individual charms that I'm sure people could point to which don't follow this rule, but they're very rare exceptions that tend to come in at the end of trees, having reached weird places by building off thematically appropriate starting points. The Infernal charmset, fun as it is to play around with, is not any of these things. There is no underlying concept tying together radiation blasts, asshole genie wish-granting, telekinesis, running really fast and weaponised shame. Solars take human skill and exaggerate it to ridiculous, extremes, Infernals do... magic stuff, which can only be made to make any sense by directly tying it back to the Yozis, which then requires several paragraphs of explanations of why the Yozis are how they are and therefore how the Infernal charmset totally makes sense. The two charmsets aren't comparable at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-12T17:46:06-08:00","id":1158035,"title":"","content":"Maybe have Yozi influence mainly appear in Shintai related abillities and upper end charms?<br /> Like, let's look at those stealth charms and ...huh. We got what appear to be melee charms? Awareness charms? I don't know what the Blood Scenting Cylcone would be tied to.<br /> Okay,<br /> First charm uses a metaphor of the Yozi's to describe what is essentially quiet stealthing.<br /> Second stealth charm brings in straight up invsibillity, but we're still stealthing. We've manipulated the world in an odd way.<br /> Third one things get...stranger. Perfect stealth while blind is strange. Basically become a guided missle(Ish?).<br /> Fourth one is something I have less reference for (I don't know what forcing people into stealth would mean?). IT's use is apparent with the second tree of charms, though.<br /> <br /> Blood Scenting Cyclone is a weirder stealth charm, and seems to take the mastery of stealth to a strange place. I would have guessed awareness, but maybe mastery of stealth as in can't be ambushed? Again, seems more awareness-y.<br /> Next on sounds like an odd awareness charm. I like it. It feels...monstrous and arrogant? Like it doesn't help you <i>find</i> people. It makes people who hide suffer.<br /> Next one has no flavor text.<br /> And fourth one in is again the weird one, with the most overt Yozi-ness. <br /> <br /> <br /> I think Infernals and Solars at <i>start</i> should feel similair. Approach things differently, maybe with the infernal forcing external changes as oppose (I note that the infernal uses externals more overtly: bending the wind, gaining iniative from other people hiding, etc), which might be an intreasting angle. But the real differences should emerge as the trees expand a bit. Hell, the expanding your conciousness to warp reality from within your soul sounds like a good take on Wyld Shaping Technique.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-12T18:08:28-08:00","id":1158044,"title":"","content":"It'd be interesting, but not really gameable (because it's basically Every Infernal an Exigent), for something like Devil Tigers (but not actually on the power scale of devil tigers - just a way of creating a being that has a primordial-like mindset and what are probably not actually second or third circle demons expressing them) to be the <i>point</i> of Infernals -<br /> The purpose of the infernal exaltation in this scenario is to shove a big fuck you up the asses of the Incarnae by creating fifty unbound quasi-yozi exalts who's powers are mostly drawn from their own themes and personalities, and their unique way of relating to the various spheres of sapient activity (Skills). They share only the most basic framework, because the primary purpose of the infernal exaltation is to deliver mostly unflavored primordial essence into a human soul along with the power of exaltation. From that only slightly influenced base, the nature of their exaltation is entirely flavored by the content of their character - and gradually becomes divorced from human aesthetics as a feedback loop forms between their identity and the power they receive from it.<br /> <br /> &quot;Fuck your god kings, have a bunch of self-defined titan kings, on roughly the same power level as those god kings.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":357,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/357-plotvitalnpc","user":"PlotVitalNPC","date":". 11-12-2017, 09:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/357-plotvitalnpc","name":"PlotVitalNPC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar357_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-12T18:47:18-08:00","id":1158048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1157439-how-complicated-should-infernals-be?p=1158035#post1158035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perfect stealth while blind is strange.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I still have some issues with the degree to which Second Edition made Adorjan a kind of murder Buddha (and the extensions given to this by fans), I do still see something a bit intriguing in the idea of a certain disruption of consciousness, and playing off of the idea that Adorjan is a notably wounded Yozi, and that being so might empower her in a way.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat actually reminds me of a consideration I once had that a unifying theme for Infernals could be an idea of being empowered by your proverbial wounds. Certainly, I think it would be a logical extension of the idea of Infernals as Chosen from the deprived and the crushed, with a notion that part of what lets the coopted Solar resonate with the Yozis is that combination of overwhelming power and having been severely put down.<br /> <br /> \u200bSo you've got something powerful that also handicaps you in a manner, and is intrinsically tied to violence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fourth one is something I have less reference for (I don't know what forcing people into stealth would mean?)\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI think that might be a turn of phrase from an earlier iteration of the rules. Either that or a more complete version would elaborate on how it forces people to make rolls to go into stealth.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe combination of that and the idea that they forget what they were doing does strike me as having an application in avoiding detection, though; the image of being able to pass through a place undetected because you made everybody else hide and then go into a slight fugue state.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And fourth one in is again the weird one, with the most overt Yozi-ness.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI find the Stealth element in that one to be how it makes the people and things you destroy with it forgotten.<br /> <br /> Looking back at those Charms, it makes me think a bit of the Exarch from Mage: the Awakening. I won't go into too much detail about them, but suffice to say that they're antagonistic deities who rules the world, with one corresponding to each of the Arcana (fundamental aspects of reality as controlled by magic).<br /> <br /> \u200bBut they're not as straightforward as the Exarch of Forces being the one in charge of the universe's energy and things, because they correspond to the Arcana by interpreting them through a lens of control and tyranny. So the Exarch of Forces is all about violence and warfare, the Exarch of Mind is all about conformity, the Exarch of Space is about surveillance and paranoia.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt makes me think about what the symbolic associations of a Yozi might be, and then interpreting an Ability through that lens. So while there are probably Stealth Charms associated with the Silent Wind because of the association with being silent and invisible, it extends into this place of interpreting Stealth through things like applications of violence.<br /> <br /> \u200bStill, on the subject of how they might have cohesion: Anubis made the point about Solar Charm cascades having distinct paths even when they weren't specifically divided into categories, and now I'm wondering how a similar thing for Infernals might work. In comparison to the Solars, where they're something like different styles or tactical avenues, you get Abilities delineated by interpretations of them through the symbolic associations of Yozis who resonate with those Abilities, and the commonality that makes them feel like part of the same Charm set are in structural elements such as including handicaps or weaknesses, empowering a wounded state, or imposing conditions on people or things around you.<br /> <br /> \u200bWhile I've expressed concern over the possibility for very many Yozis to add excessive complication, I should also note that I feel that a variety of aesthetics and applications even within a single Ability would be a worthwhile means of expressing Infernal themes and distinguishing them. I would view that variety as a feature, and a means of making them eldritch, in much the same way as a sorcerer with a variety of spells would be expressing power through a number of aesthetics. I would be inclined to encourage drawing on that variety, both as a way of making them look weirded and emphasizing that theme of excess, and in distancing them from any specific Yozi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-12T19:07:29-08:00","id":1158053,"title":"","content":"Based on the tidbits Neall and Vance have dropped (including the completely reimagined Caste names and marks), I anticipate Infernals in 3e being more like Solars than not, varying from them to a similar degree that Abyssals do. <br /> <br /> That is, they will still generally be about doing human things, just better than mortals, with a twist of lime. <br /> <br /> The way their Castes are mirrors of Solars from an external perspective suggests that they may have a theme of winning through hampering, e.g., you won the foot race because you made everyone else slower; as contrasted with a Solar, who won just because they were faster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11690-mizzlfoshizzl","name":"mizzlfoshizzl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11690_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-12T19:15:44-08:00","id":1158055,"title":"","content":"To actually answer the thread question now (kind of, in a roundabout ranty way), I'm quite fond of the idea that in any charmset you should, in a perfect world, be able to point at a charm and say that this is what [Splat] <i>is</i>. If the world were ending and you were tasked with leaving behind a record of Exalted for future generations to rediscover, but due to space constraints you could only show them one charm per splat, which one would you pick as a blueprint for this whole Exalt? And I love Avoidance Kata as an example of this. It's a wonderful, iconic Sidereal charm that sums up what the Sidereals are and what they do. It's a weird effect that you wouldn't expect out of the dodge tree, but it is clearly a dodge charm, it's just approaching the concept of dodging from an unexpected direction. There's a lot of other stuff that Sidereals do which you couldn't reverse-engineer from Avoidance Kata, but if future civilisations saw that oddly lateral, powerful but very specific, mysterious reality-warping charm and tried to build a whole splat from it, what they made would capture the essence of the splat and feel like Sidereals even if it was markedly different in a lot of ways.<br /> <br /> For Solars I'd similarly go with a dodge charm in the form of Seven Shadow Evasion. It's a demonstration of ridiculously superhuman ability - you're so good at dodging that if everything everywhere exploded all at once, you'd comfortably slide off to the side and somehow come out of it unharmed. If you start with a clear and direct expression of unimaginable prowess, whatever our wasteland-dwelling descendents make is going to feel a lot like the Solars of today. Trying to come up with these splat-defining charms obviously isn't a perfect test of a charmset by any means, but I like it as a fun thought experiment that helps with mapping out the essential themes of a splat.<br /> <br /> Infernals don't have anything like this, and that, even more than anything in the first two chapters of their book, has always been my least favourite part of them. I'm perfectly fine with a splat being complex, but having a clear concept to tie all of that complexity together and turn it into a distinct thing with its own character matters a lot to me. The basic conceit of drawing from a bunch of entirely different, self-contained charmsets makes it all but impossible to have an answer to the question of &quot;what do Infernals do?&quot;, but even within individual Yozi trees there isn't always a clear theme. It's really hard to find some connecting concept between sandbending and drawing power from prayer.<br /> <br /> What <i>could </i>be the underlying theme of the Infernals is our old friend Triumphant Howl of the Devil-Tiger. The idea of reforging yourself and the world around you with your own force of will and becoming your own legend is very cool, and might be something you can try to build a charmset around. That said, despite the prominence it has in internet discourse around the Infernals, it's not and never was the theme of Infernals outside of fanon. Devil-Tigering only exists in the last few pages of the Broken-Winged Crane, it isn't even hinted at anywhere else in the Infernal charmset, so making it a central theme would require extensive rejiggering. It'd be really hard to build an actual charmset centred around the concept, as opposed to making it a free pass for people to go make up their own charms, but my ideal 3e Infernals would be somehow based around the Devil-Tiger idea or some other thematically resonant concept appropriate to Infernals, rather than based around the Yozis. The themes of the Yozis would then be seen in the charmset through that lens, being the awesome embodiment of your own legend in Malfean or Cecelynian ways, for instance. Or maybe taking the backer preview approach and being a gloriously degenerate returned god-king in Malfean or Cecelynian ways, if that's the central Infernal theme you decide to pursue. Absolutely no idea how you would actually do that, though, so this may all be a wildly unrealistic dream.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":3559,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","user":"Lanaya","date":". 11-12-2017, 10:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-12T19:19:42-08:00","id":1158056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1157439-how-complicated-should-infernals-be?p=1158055#post1158055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What <i>could </i>be the underlying theme of the Infernals is our old friend Triumphant Howl of the Devil-Tiger. The idea of reforging yourself and the world around you with your own force of will and becoming your own legend is very cool, and might be something you can try to build a charmset around. That said, despite the prominence it has in internet discourse around the Infernals, it's not and never was the theme of Infernals outside of fanon. Devil-Tigering only exists in the last few pages of the Broken-Winged Crane, it isn't even hinted at anywhere else in the Infernal charmset. It'd be really hard to build an actual charmset centred around the concept, as opposed to making it a free pass for people to go make up their own charms, but my ideal 3e Infernals would be somehow based around the Devil-Tiger idea or some other thematically resonant concept appropriate to Infernals, rather than based around the Yozis. The themes of the Yozis would then be seen in the charmset through that lens, being the awesome embodiment of your own legend in Malfean or Cecelynian ways, for instance. Or maybe taking the backer preview approach and being a gloriously degenerate returned god-king in Malfean or Cecelynian ways, if that's the central Infernal theme you decide to pursue. Absolutely no idea how you would actually do that, though, so this may all be a wildly unrealistic dream.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know how crazy of a dream it is, given the description of making a paradise out of the depths of your soul.<br /> <br /> \u200bHonestly, I think this and the above mentioned by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/357-plotvitalnpc\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar357_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"357\" data-vbnamecard=\"357\">PlotVitalNPC</a> are a tad more probable then theorized. Not exactly the same, mind, but given that Infernals have Shintais, a unique-to-them-as-people boss form, and that Infernal charms have a history of shaping their users(Although Vance has said those would be opt-in charms), and the idea of making demons out of you and warping reality to fit your soul, I'd say it's a decent subtheme there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-12T19:36:03-08:00","id":1158058,"title":"","content":"(hmm, to keep it on topic...)<br /> <br /> \u200bIf I have concerns that a large number and variety of Yozis would make Infernals too complicated, then I definitely think adding in stuff to do with some highly empowered self-definition would.<br /> <br /> \u200bI also feel that whatever Infernals are, they should feel as though they warrant the term.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat's part of why I like the association with green fire; it's just familiar enough for the necessary association, but hints at something a bit weird and different.<br /> <br /> \u200bAlthough that does put me in mind of a possible flaw in ParanoiaCombo's point; excessive familiarity with the Yozis being required is an issue, but I suspect that one needs to be at least a bit familiar with the game's take on Hell to be able to make full sense of what is hellish in these Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-12T20:02:43-08:00","id":1158063,"title":"","content":"Although, even if I'm one who thinks that a certain degree of complexity is a feature, I wonder if there's only so much room in a given character for a number of them, and if there should be a restraining mechanism similar to Second Edition with its repurchasing Excellencies.<br /> <br /> \u200bOr would that be as simple as just being limited in how many Charms you could ever really afford?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-12T21:26:11-08:00","id":1158073,"title":"","content":"...I have trouble seeing how this is complicated.<br /> You list the themes of the Yozi in question, develop charms for them, then divide them into charm trees based on Abilities.Rinse and repeat for the next Yozi. Trim the fat after you are done (so you don't have 6 charms that do the same thing), check that certain Abilities are not neglected after the fact.<br /> <br /> Yes, this could well be very complex but hardly more so than Solars. The more esoteric charms are locked behind Shintai keywords, and having more than one Yozi contribute to an Ability can give us a taste of the weird mutant demon kings that 2nd introduced us too.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-13T05:28:08-08:00","id":1158140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1157439-how-complicated-should-infernals-be?p=1158073#post1158073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rinse and repeat for the next Yozi.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bAnd the next one, and the next one, and the next, until there are what? 15, 23, more?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-13T05:33:31-08:00","id":1158142,"title":"","content":"The book could present a few yozi trees for each ability while making it clear that other such trees exist for different yozi, including those you homebrew yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-13T08:27:55-08:00","id":1158176,"title":"","content":"I'll note that an answer of &quot;in practice, don't actually write very many Yozis into the Infernal Charm set&quot; constitutes a stand on how complex they ought to be all its own.<br /> <br /> \u200bOn the other hand, I'd say it needs to be reconciled with a statement from a developer that making them Ability based opens up the exciting possibility of being able to add things like inspiration from Isidoros or Szoreny. Add those two to the five that definitely need to be there from the outset, and one is already dealing with the possibility of significant complication.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-13T08:45:59-08:00","id":1158181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1157439-how-complicated-should-infernals-be?p=1158176#post1158176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll note that an answer of &quot;in practice, don't actually write very many Yozis into the Infernal Charm set&quot; constitutes a stand on how complex they ought to be all its own.<br /> <br /> \u200bOn the other hand, I'd say it needs to be reconciled with a statement from a developer that making them Ability based opens up the exciting possibility of being able to add things like inspiration from Isidoros or Szoreny. Add those two to the five that definitely need to be there from the outset, and one is already dealing with the possibility of significant complication.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So I thought on this a bit, specifically adding more Yozi's when we have so much of the big 5+1. <br /> I think we're not getting more Yozis, which sets us to 15 Yozis.(Malfeas, Ceceylne, SWLIHN, Adjoran, Ebon Dragon, Kimbery, Qaf, Isodoros, Szorney, Cytherea, Oramous, Metagagos, Elloge, Sachrevall, Hegera). <br /> I also think that there needs to be more equilbirium of themes. We had a whole charm set built on 5+1 of these guys. Either the other 9~ need to be expanded into just as wide a conceptual space...or the 5(And maybe the +1 kimbery) need to shrink and become more tight and focused. <br /> <br /> Going back to the Abyssal comparison, I think that shrinking and focusing the Big 5 might be the way to go. Malfeas doesn't need to show up in <i>every </i>combat tree. Ceclyne can maybe cede some conceptual space to Qaf as spiritual leader of the Yozi. Etc. Of course, you'd still want a common theme to their charms, an identiy shared by the Infernals that links all the concepts of the Yozi together. But that's a space that's kinda wide open it seems to me. I'd like something about hubris or decadence or self-motivation/definition or the like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-13T10:57:03-08:00","id":1158218,"title":"","content":"I'm considering the possibility in something that might create incentives for actual Infernal player characters to limit the number of Abilities that they might go heavily into.<br /> <br /> Solars have a fairly good balance between generalisation and specialisation between Supernal Ability and a lot of powerful, inviting Essence 1 Charms, so a Solar's player generally always has room to expand vertically or laterally as suits them and their character concept.<br /> <br /> \u200bI think the idea of the expansive, multifaceted Charm set might be an argument against Infernals having anything like Supernal, and would complicate making the roots of every Ability inviting to them. So I wonder if instead, they might benefit from some kind of system in which the expansive nature of each Ability means that they get a decent amount of breadth even if they're only developing a comparatively small number of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-13T11:06:35-08:00","id":1158221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1157439-how-complicated-should-infernals-be?p=1158181#post1158181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> or the 5(And maybe the +1 kimbery) need to shrink and become more tight and focused.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be part of why I've asked around dropping the part of Malfeas designating him as king of the Primordials.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe description in the preview gave me that sense of themes in Abilities resonating with themes in Yozis when it talked about Brawl having Charms resembling Malfeas through the idea of that fighting channelling the character's rage, so I think that might be a decent basis for deciding which combat does and does not resonate with Malfeas. Brawl and Melee are good candidates, while Archery, Thrown and War feel a bit less so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">self-motivation/definition</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI feel as though self-definition is a bit of a vague and circular parameter, and doesn't really feel like part of the Yozis if they're being divested of aspects that were added in the first place to create that narrative of turning into them.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt's like... the metaphysical concept behind the Ebon Dragon having a Charm whose function is to state &quot;I am the Ebon Dragon&quot; is kind of neat, but still primarily serves as a means for a theoretical Essence 10 character to become the Ebon Dragon. In a system and setting that has set aside both the idea of such elaboration on a Yozi, and the idea of providing such a hard mechanical road map to the upper end of character possibilities, does it really make as much sense?<br /> <br /> I'm speaking primarily in terms of argument against it as a unifying foundation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-13T11:36:15-08:00","id":1158234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1157439-how-complicated-should-infernals-be?p=1158221#post1158221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bI feel as though self-definition is a bit of a vague and circular parameter, and doesn't really feel like part of the Yozis if they're being divested of aspects that were added in the first place to create that narrative of turning into them.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt's like... the metaphysical concept behind the Ebon Dragon having a Charm whose function is to state &quot;I am the Ebon Dragon&quot; is kind of neat, but still primarily serves as a means for a theoretical Essence 10 character to become the Ebon Dragon. In a system and setting that has set aside both the idea of such elaboration on a Yozi, and the idea of providing such a hard mechanical road map to the upper end of character possibilities, does it really make as much sense?<br /> <br /> I'm speaking primarily in terms of argument against it as a unifying foundation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm...I can see that. I guess the sorta-Ubermensch sounding charms from 2e are still changing my thinking. I'm re-reading Ink Monkeys today to look for a better foundation.<br /> I'd suggest Shintai might provide the hook Supernal did, especially with it granting weird/cool powers early.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-13T13:50:27-08:00","id":1158267,"title":"","content":"Alright spent sometime reading the Ink Monkey's stuff on the Yozi. And an intreasting commonality I noticed is powers that effect things...passively.<br /> <br /> Like, interacting with the Yozi's is a transformative experience, in a way that feels kinda unique. I think that sort of alteration of others could be an intreasting space for Infernals to explore. I'm trying to nail down how that would work, but I think the effect on the surrounding by merely being there might be intreasting, captsontes imposing permanent effects (like adjoran's removing the memory of someone. SWLIHN altering the midn through implanting her name. And so on.).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T07:05:39-08:00","id":1158450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1157439-how-complicated-should-infernals-be?p=1158073#post1158073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...I have trouble seeing how this is complicated.<br /> You list the themes of the Yozi in question, develop charms for them, then divide them into charm trees based on Abilities.Rinse and repeat for the next Yozi. Trim the fat after you are done (so you don't have 6 charms that do the same thing), check that certain Abilities are not neglected after the fact.<br /> <br /> Yes, this could well be very complex but hardly more so than Solars. The more esoteric charms are locked behind Shintai keywords, and having more than one Yozi contribute to an Ability can give us a taste of the weird mutant demon kings that 2nd introduced us too.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, this is basically my point as well. <br /> <br /> The solar charmset already draws from dozens of different inspirations. Like I pointed out, the athletics tree alone draws from multiple different themes/sources and that's one out of 25 abilities. <br /> <br /> If you're only drawing from 15 different themes (16 if you count infernals as their own theme) you're actually vastly <i>reducing</i> the complexity of the charmset. I really think this whole thread is tilting at windmills.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T07:56:15-08:00","id":1158470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1157439-how-complicated-should-infernals-be?p=1158450#post1158450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> the athletics tree alone draws from multiple different <b>themes</b>/sources and that's one out of 25 abilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>What are the different themes that it's drawing on?<br /> <br /> \u200bBecause, while it's drawing on different sources to be sure, the fact that all of those sources ultimately amount to &quot;being really good at athletics&quot;, so I greatly doubt that the end result feels particularly discordant to most people.<br /> <br /> \u200bSure, Heracles never actually leaps about rooftops or stands atop narrow poles in his original mythology or most of the things that adapt it, but if he did, I don't think it would feel massively out of place compared to any of his other displays of athletic prowess.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're only drawing from 15 different themes (16 if you count infernals as their own theme)</div> </div> </div> </div>Describe those themes to me, as you see them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T09:15:45-08:00","id":1158500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1157439-how-complicated-should-infernals-be?p=1158470#post1158470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What are the different themes that it's drawing on?<br /> <br /> \u200bBecause, while it's drawing on different sources to be sure, the fact that all of those sources ultimately amount to &quot;being really good at athletics&quot;, so I greatly doubt that the end result feels particularly discordant to most people.<br /> <br /> \u200bSure, Heracles never actually leaps about rooftops or stands atop narrow poles in his original mythology or most of the things that adapt it, but if he did, I don't think it would feel massively out of place compared to any of his other displays of athletic prowess.</div> </div> </div> </div>And see here's the thing. You keep saying that they're all a cohesive whole, and that they all follow a central theme and they're all outpourings of that except... they aren't. Not by default, anyway. They are a cohesive whole that makes sense as a cohesive whole because the writers and devs have poured <i>hours</i> into making sure they all have the same feel. <br /> <br /> If they were all <i>just </i>&quot;really good at X&quot; then the solar charmset would stop at the excellencies. There is nothing about being really good at swordsmanship that allows you to magically manifest a golden sword made out of your own power. If Solar Survival automatically lent itself to training an animal to such extents that they became a building-sized engine of destruction and awesome power then why wasn't there <i>anything </i>even remotely similar in 2E? <br /> <br /> All of the Solar charms are inspired by external sources. And no, all of those sources are not &quot;just being really good at something&quot; because most of what the solar exalted do is literally impossible. <br /> <br /> I'm not just making this up completely either. Solars aren't just 'doing things really good' From the Ask the Devs thread:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1144744#post1144744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The aesthetics of a Charmset are typically gradated through its progression. For example, <b>both Solar and Dragon-Blooded Charms at the lower end begin as expressions of superhuman skill, but Solars progress towards embodying the divine perfection of the Unconquered Sun </b>while the Dragon-Blooded progress towards overt manipulation of elements and embodiment of elemental Essence.<br /> <br /> Lunar Charms begin as expressions of superhuman Attributes - the incredible strength of the hulking berserker, the the deceptive wiles of the fox-tailed trickster, the shaman's keen eye that can see the invisible. They progress towards expressions of the Lunar's nature as divine apex predators - the inescapable pursuit of the hunting god-beast, devouring demons and fae and digesting their Charms, turning the strength of the wolf to protect your chosen mortal flock.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bolding mine. <br /> <br /> Note that it's only at the lower end of the charmset that the solars are all about expressions of superhuman skill. Much the same, I anticipate that only at the lower end of their charmsets will the infernals emulate the yozis directly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1157439-how-complicated-should-infernals-be?p=1158470#post1158470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Describe those themes to me, as you see them.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only reason you'd be asking me this is you're trying to mock me by implying that I don't understand the amount of complexity/lack of complexity that each Yozi has under their names. Regardless, it's a silly question. Go read Games of Divinity or the Ink Monkey treatise on the Lesser known Yozi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T09:23:54-08:00","id":1158508,"title":"","content":"Vances quote does point to a problem, though. <br /> Solars are based on 1 model(ucs)<br /> Lunars have 1 (Luna)<br /> Sidereal have 5 or 1( maidens, or fate)<br /> Abyssals have 13(deathlird) united by asthetic choice and gothic themes.<br /> Dragonblooded are in the sid boat(5 dragons)<br /> <br /> The yozi probably have a derivable commonality. But it's not obscured then the rest and makes the task of finding &quot;how&quot; of unity a bit harder. It's not as apparent(yet) compared to the Maidens, Dragons, and Deathlprds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T09:57:03-08:00","id":1158527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1157439-how-complicated-should-infernals-be?p=1158500#post1158500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they were all <i>just </i>&quot;really good at X&quot; then the solar charmset would stop at the excellencies.</div> </div> </div> </div>No it wouldn't; as is evident in the resulting Charms, it would expand from there to areas of increased refinement and efficiency, such as rerolling 6s and doubling dice numbers other than 10, and various other things that are expressions of superhuman application of those Abilities that would not be expressed by numbers of successes. Crossing a mountain in a single bound is still an expression of superhuman athletic skill, and no number of successes on a normal dice roll will accomplish that.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe divine perfection of the Unconquered Sun generally expresses itself as superhuman skill in any case.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Solar Survival automatically lent itself to training an animal to such extents that they became a building-sized engine of destruction and awesome power then why wasn't there <i>anything </i>even remotely similar in 2E?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because nobody bothered.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">All of the Solar charms are inspired by external sources.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI don't really agree with that, but it's not exactly relevant, because they're still not sources that are massively dissimilar from each other.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And no, all of those sources are not &quot;just being really good at something&quot; because most of what the solar exalted do is literally impossible.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a false dichotomy; crossing a mountain in a single leap is literally impossible, but still an expression of superhuman athletic capability.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note that it's only at the lower end of the charmset that the solars are all about expressions of superhuman skill. Much the same, I anticipate that only at the lower end of their charmsets will the infernals emulate the yozis directly.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThat strikes me as being the wrong way around.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only reason you'd be asking me this is you're trying to mock me by implying that I don't understand the amount of complexity/lack of complexity that each Yozi has under their names. Regardless, it's a silly question.</div> </div> </div> </div>You keep coming into this thread, in which I have asked a question, and keep asserting that the question doesn't pertain to anything real by vaguely gesturing at a self-evident cohesion in Yozi themes or statements that Solars are even more disparate and complex because they have things like being able to run and jump. I'm trying to get you to actually lay out the Yozis in a way that would actually back this up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Go read Games of Divinity or the Ink Monkey treatise on the Lesser known Yozi.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bIn Games of Divinity, we have the grinding, burning metal city of raw hatred, the infinitely stretching desert of ruin and oppression, the mass of crystalline spheres who deal in mind-control and social engineering, the gigantic shadow driven to escape schemes and enamoured of doom, and the sound-dampening murder wind.<br /> <br /> Aesthetically and thematically, they're a bit more diverse than various renditions of human beings doing their thing to exaggerated extremes, or even the fiery golden paragon of people doing their thing to exaggerated extremes.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T10:13:38-08:00","id":1158534,"title":"","content":"I just wanted to pop in to say I agree with almost everything Isator is saying. Which means there's not much point me saying the same thing.<br /> Carry on Isator. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, what Epee102 was just saying about the multiplicity of power-sources and the need for something unifying, which is a bit difficult to find.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T17:09:39-08:00","id":1158711,"title":"","content":"Conintuing on that, I think there _are_ some intreasting themes with Yozis. They take some digging though.<br /> <br /> The Yozis all passively change those around them(SWLIHHN brainwashes, Isodorious breaks mirrors by trodding, Oraumus...<i>is,</i> and so one).<br /> The Yozis are all broken in a key capacity from where they were.<br /> The Yozis warp reality around them in singular ways that are a bit...weird. Mainly thinking of Metagagos here, but Elloge does it too.<br /> The Yozis are inhospitable to mortal life by their presence, and thus can only be dealt with from afar.<br /> The Yozis induce their compulsions on others (Hegera's rains of emotion, Adjoran's silence, Qaf's enlightment, Metagagos and the swamp spreading, Oramus's maddness).<br /> <br /> So, how complicated do Infernals <i>need</i> to be? Not very, I think. The fifteen paths can all, I believe, be connected somehow. I don't know how <i>yet</i>. But I don't beleive it's impossilbe. Especially if tied to archetypal notions of decadent demon kings. <br /> <br /> I've liked Hubris and Decadence as themes of the new infenral themes(Mainly cuz I can tie a large number of diverse cultural characters into infernals that way, with Ravanna, Ganondorf, Mezentius, albiet I'd need to work to incorporate more heroes). But I'd rather wait to see more before pinning them down outside of hypothetical homeberws.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T00:39:46-08:00","id":1158799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1157439-how-complicated-should-infernals-be?p=1158711#post1158711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Conintuing on that, I think there _are_ some intreasting themes with Yozis. They take some digging though.<br /> <br /> The Yozis all passively change those around them(SWLIHHN brainwashes, Isodorious breaks mirrors by trodding, Oraumus...<i>is,</i> and so one).<br /> The Yozis are all broken in a key capacity from where they were.<br /> The Yozis warp reality around them in singular ways that are a bit...weird. Mainly thinking of Metagagos here, but Elloge does it too.<br /> The Yozis are inhospitable to mortal life by their presence, and thus can only be dealt with from afar.<br /> The Yozis induce their compulsions on others (Hegera's rains of emotion, Adjoran's silence, Qaf's enlightment, Metagagos and the swamp spreading, Oramus's maddness).<br /> <br /> So, how complicated do Infernals <i>need</i> to be? Not very, I think. The fifteen paths can all, I believe, be connected somehow. I don't know how <i>yet</i>. But I don't beleive it's impossilbe. Especially if tied to archetypal notions of decadent demon kings.<br /> <br /> I've liked Hubris and Decadence as themes of the new infenral themes(Mainly cuz I can tie a large number of diverse cultural characters into infernals that way, with Ravanna, Ganondorf, Mezentius, albiet I'd need to work to incorporate more heroes). But I'd rather wait to see more before pinning them down outside of hypothetical homeberws.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, I think that's the sort of thing that can be brought across their charmset without feeling like you've got 10-15 thematically distinct power sets rammed into one character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T22:13:33-07:00","id":1387415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1157439-how-complicated-should-infernals-be?p=1158140#post1158140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bAnd the next one, and the next one, and the next, until there are what? 15, 23, more?</div> </div> </div> </div>I know I shouldn't, but I've chosen to respond to your direct question.<br /> Short answer; yes.<br /> <br /> Longer answer; if you need too. You only need so many charms for a character, or a group there of. Even if you go with say 5 themes per Yozi, making at least 1 per ability (115*25=2875) and keep the duplicate effects (maybe allow the choosing of a Shintai keyword once per purchase and some cosmetic differences), which I freely admit is upping the complexity...you won't need that many charms. You won't want to write them and most people will gloss over the majority anyway (sadly). That including Shintai charms, if those are going to be a thing. So yes, it can be complex.<br /> <br /> But in practice, some of those themes just aren't applicable to every ability. I can see the Ebon Dragon create a Melee Charm enhancing a feint gambit (sneaky, treachery, etc) but I can't see a Malfeas charm in Stealth. It is VERY important to remember that they don't have to be. Nor do the Infernals even need to use the caste ability list of the Solars. Infernals get their own design space, with their own designated elements, strengths and weaknesses. Look at the cool weirdness in 3e Lunars and Dragonblooded and see how their general outlines let their themes shine in individual charms. Do we really need SWLIHN to have a Dodge charm? It just isn't relevant to her. Malfeas getting a Performance charm that substitutes Performance for Dodge is much more interesting and flavourful. Meanwhile Cecelyne can have a Performance charm that enhances prayer, possible even two way comunication with spirit in question, with an upgrade at higher Essence that allows the Exalt to hear and respond to prayers directed at them. Different Yozi, different themes, same ability.<br /> <br /> The issue is that the themes are represented, not that they are everywhere. Malfeas doen't need that many dancing Charms. If a theme isn't that important or useful to charm design, it doesn't even have to be used. Heck, this is a new edition, the Yozi may have different themes! I'm not against the Infernals having their own themes separate from the Yozi, but I would like the Yozi's themes to echo through the Green Sun Princes both to drive home the connection between the two and because it is simpler to connect the those elements to charm design than generate whole new ones and colour them in after. Yes the charmset i am imaging would be a mishmash of different themes (from different Yozi) spread across all the abilities. I can see how this can create some thematic conflict with infernal characters if we just take Yozi themes apply them individually and let people pick up conflicting themes in said characters.<br /> <br /> And it is beautiful.<br /> <br /> Yozi might not be charm engine primordials anymore, but they are concepts &amp; themes bound into living worlds who clash and compromise in order to create anything lasting outside of the Wyld or themselves. Someone should struggle to reconcile trying to be both the Ebon Dragon, She Who Lives In Her Name and Isidoros all at the same time<br /> That is part of why I do like some of the ideas being discussed. The concept that Yozi inspired charms are revelatory and transformative is brilliant. It even plays into my ideal infernal charmset. What have you learned? How has it changed you? Likewise I do enjoy reading your posts <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar158_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"158\" data-vbnamecard=\"158\">Isator Levi</a>. I find your perspective to be occasionally enlightening and always interesting.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure I can in good faith contribute positively to the discussion, so I'll bow out for now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T00:54:43-07:00","id":1387433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1157439-how-complicated-should-infernals-be?p=1158176#post1158176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...making them Ability based opens up the exciting possibility of being able to add things like inspiration from Isidoros or Szoreny.</div> </div> </div> </div>This bit puts me in mind of the Terrestrial and Mastery keywords in Martial Arts charms. Perhaps a certain Athletics charm could have X effect, with the keyword &quot;Isidoros,&quot; meaning that an Infernal associated with Isidoros would enjoy additional effect Y when using this charm.<br /> <br /> Not sure how useful that is, it's just something that occurred to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1856-hakkonen","name":"Hakkonen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T02:06:22-07:00","id":1387436,"title":"","content":"With a whole bunch of Yozis to choose from, that's a lot of wordcount for something that most Infernals won't be able to access.<br /> <br /> If you wanted to have Infernals associate with a particular Yozi and gain benefits for that, I'd suggest that favouring all your Yozi's charms is a better solution.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T02:12:22-07:00","id":1387437,"title":"","content":"I'll be honest FallenEco, while that sounds kind of interesting on paper, I just found that Infernals having a mish-mash of themes just did not work well at all, and in fact I'd say most of the Infernal characters I played with I can't even remember, they were such poor characters. The only one I remember well is the one who kept rigidly to Malfean green fire and Cecylene's worship charms, because her themes were actually distinct.<br /> <br /> I was really excited to play Infernals, but in practice I was quite disappointed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T02:14:42-07:00","id":1387438,"title":"","content":"I'd also say that, by expanding the list of Yozis to 10, 15 or even 25, this'd be even worse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T02:42:16-07:00","id":1387440,"title":"","content":"The Yozi list is 13 iirc, since it will be all currently named Yozi. (Malfeas, Qaf, She Who Lives In Her Name, Elloge, Oramus, The Ebon Dragon, Cecylene, Kimbery, Metagagos, Isodorios, Szorney, Adjoran, Cyntherea.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T04:56:18-07:00","id":1387447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1157439-how-complicated-should-infernals-be?p=1387440#post1387440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Yozi list is 13 iirc, since it will be all currently named Yozi. (Malfeas, Qaf, She Who Lives In Her Name, Elloge, Oramus, The Ebon Dragon, Cecylene, Kimbery, Metagagos, Isodorios, Szorney, Adjoran, Cyntherea.)</div> </div> </div> </div>15, including Hegra and Sacheverell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T05:58:37-07:00","id":1387464,"title":"","content":"1: This thread was three years old.<br /> <br /> 2: Yozi Charms are lame, and bring in the same aesthetic limits and drawbacks as DB Charms (Want to be a Fire Brawler? You get two Charms. An Air Brawler? One.). Infernals should have <i>Infernal Charms</i>, not in the image of the Yozis, but representative of their own nature as mad sorcerer-queens, unshackled overmen, and full-on JRPG bosses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T06:18:34-07:00","id":1387467,"title":"","content":"I find them to be interesting in theory, as something to read, but in game terms I agree with you about the limitations.<br /> <br /> I was thinking some more about the other splats. Lunars aren't really about being Gaia's lover, living on the Moon, per-se. Nor are Solars about having 4 arms or carrying a laurel wreath. Alchemicals aren't about being spherical and having robo-cancer and hating your family. Dragonblood aren't, despite the name, about being dragons.<br /> <br /> The point is really to have different kind of heroes, drawing inspiration from different mythos. Lunars are Moon-heroes, inspired by lycanthropes and so on. Solars are culture and mortal/demigod heroes. Abyssals draw their themes from vampires, mummies, liches, necromancers, Dracula, etc, not from He Who Holds In Thrall and Abhorrence of Life.<br /> <br /> Yes, in-setting, Solars draw their power-theme from the Unconquered Sun, but in reality they have Larceny charms so you can play the greatest pulp thief, not because the UCS is really good at Larceny. <br /> <br /> Essentially, Infernals should draw their themes from the things the Yozis draw from; the Greek Titans, Vedic demons, Cthulu-esque elder god-themes, the Chinese Underworld, Indo-European and Mesopotamian primordial chaos serpents, Mesopotamian mythology, ancient Jewish apocalypticism, etc. And throw in some green demonfire and Western occultism, sure.<br /> <br /> But I don't think the writers should be saying &quot;Isidorus is a boar-singularity so we should write charms for that&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 05-11-2020, 09:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T07:05:14-07:00","id":1387479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1157439-how-complicated-should-infernals-be?p=1387447#post1387447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 15, including Hegra and Sacheverell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Knew I forgot some. Anyway. The charms of the Infernals should have some Yozi imagery, but we know they have charms that aren\u2019t directly Yozi based, and they have clear themes of \u201cthe broken and downtrodden rising up to burn or remake a Creation that spited them\u201d. Green fire, songs that stop thoughts, lessons that are toxic to learn, and more can fit those without getting too far afield.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T07:15:56-07:00","id":1387481,"title":"","content":"It sounds like the Infernal charms are going to related to the Yozis similarly to how the Abyssal charms are related to the deathlords.<br /> <br /> Which we also haven't seen yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T08:18:10-07:00","id":1387499,"title":"","content":"By sheer chance, Vance just now happened to mention in the Discord that Cytherea and Sacheverell won't feature in the Infernal Charmset. (I'd guess setting reasons, probably; Sach is asleep and Cytherea is supposed to be a mystery.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T08:31:41-07:00","id":1387504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1157439-how-complicated-should-infernals-be?p=1387499#post1387499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By sheer chance, Vance just now happened to mention in the Discord that Cytherea and Sacheverell won't feature in the Infernal Charmset. (I'd guess setting reasons, probably; Sach is asleep and Cytherea is supposed to be a mystery.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh thank heavens I loathed Cytherea. Sach is a _bit_ suprising, but I figure some dream-based charms are plausible.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Wonder if they tried making their own...exalts. THat'd be interesitng.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T10:31:57-07:00","id":1387539,"title":"","content":"I don't find &quot;Yozis Charms&quot; lame or not lame exactly but....<br /> <br /> The Yozis are to me not, at their heart, things that are like &quot;mechanisms&quot; or &quot;robots&quot; which are &quot;made&quot; of &quot;Charm mechanics&quot; which somehow literally and absolutely define them and which can only be applied in an exactly rigid and formula following manner by their Chosen.<br /> <br /> They are made of mad, flowing, vainglorious power and monomaniacal principle which will flow as how it chooses, and which flow through the hands of their chosen as and when they choose, according to improvisation, caprice and whim, bound only by their internal passions.<br /> <br /> Sidereals inspired some of the design for the Infernals in having rigid Charms which players have to be clever to get the most out of.<br /> <br /> &quot;Rigid Charms, which players have fun subverting&quot; makes sense for the Sidereals - bureaucrats bound by rules and seers bound by Fate, that *should*, by all that is right and planned by Heaven's will, inhibit their ability to make things work out mostly as they please rather than as it must (and yet, and yet...)<br /> <br /> But for the Yozis Chosen? (I mean, they're not exactly moe-robot papa Autochthon, who might actually, if anything is, be feasibly made of rigid, mechanical magic-forms that *literally* exist in the world of the setting...).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T11:04:33-07:00","id":1387543,"title":"","content":"I honestly really liked 2nd ed's infernals, I want something that showcases inhuman monsters warped by the outsiders that are so vast and powerful their mere presence creates and warps reality. I would like more examples of heretic charms that bridge the gaps between various yozi and I think the yozi had way to much involvement in the infernals which should have more come from the yozi's various souls instead of the yozi directly and that doesn't even mention the shit show that lilun was and I always homebrewed her as something other than what was presented along with how the yozi treated the infernals upon reaching the demon city.<br /> <br /> the only problem with building this way is that the infernals become an &quot;advanced&quot; class of solar to play where you need to know a lot about charm balance and how to homebrew or the devs would literally need to put out a supplement to help teach people how to balance homebrew","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T12:56:00-07:00","id":1387575,"title":"","content":"You know, much as I dislike this kind of thread necromancy, of all thread I can say that this is one that at least has some basis for revival, since in the time since it was first discussed we've gotten two more Exalted Charm sets to serve as a basis for speculation on how those kinds of things can work.<br /> <br /> But that's not really a subject of concern to myself at the moment.<br /> <br /> It's a funny thing that a Wikipedia search of the topic of stomach rumblings made on a whim should ultimately lead me to the topic of the subculture in 17th century France of fortune tellers who also engaged in practices of poisoning, abortions and supposedly even the provision of Black Masses. The logic goes that they would start off learning what it was that their clientele hoped would be predicted for them and ultimately lead to the purpose of alternately providing potions of varying effectiveness to achieve those ends (then as now most such people would seek advice for grievances of love and rivalry) or outright claiming that they could perform ceremonies allowing the Devil to be entreated to bestow their heart's desire.<br /> <br /> There have been times in the past where I've been sceptical of the idea of Satanism in terms of people actually knowingly worshipping a deity that stands for evil, and that still doesn't seem to be the case. It looks more like... the right kinds of people can be conned into believing that their desires are being unmet by God, and thus there's an impulse to see if the opposition might provide for them instead. In cases such as that, it might be that the pageantry and invocation of the taboo is all about overwhelming the mark with the grandeur of it all in a manner that suckers them in (while also conveniently being such a violation of social norms that it can be hard to report having been swindled). It certainly seems to contribute a lot to the image of Satanists featured in a lot of more recent horror fiction. It's the kind of thing that I've often imagined to be the practical basis of Yozi worship in the setting, and even the message given to and promoted by the Infernal Exalted themselves; that Heaven takes you for granted, while Hell is ready to take you under its wing.<br /> <br /> And that image of infernal symbolism as a perversion of the norm that seems to pass you by, something about that struck a chord to me as what could be the structure of the Green Sun Princes.<br /> <br /> Each Solar Ability kind of portrays its own little miniature heroic narrative. The difference between Melee and Brawl isn't just in the weapon they use, there's a distinct but related personality to either of them; Melee is a bit more serene and precise, Brawl has things like pulling out hearts to incinerate in your fist. They all have a character that, even if it doesn't necessarily constrain the kinds of people that uses them, provides motifs to inform their design and make them easier to grasp.<br /> <br /> The developers still refer to Infernals as a twisted distortion of the Solars, and it makes me wonder if that could not work down to the level of the Abilities; take the driving character underlying each one and figure out a personality that would come across as a version that is subversive, appropriated to a more callous or self-involved nature or given particularly violent and domineering extremes. Within that structure, the aesthetics of the Yozis are merely the means of achieving that personality, rather than the personality in their own right. The alter might be decked out with a statue of Baphomet, black candles and skulls, but they're not really the object of worship they're just representative of the taboo that you're trying to thrive within.<br /> <br /> I think that kind of thing could ideally make the Green Sun Princes feel cohesive while their power covers a variety of divergent forms.<br /> <br /> One could even derive a point of theme from the idea that these are Yozi qualities subordinated to the image of the dread sorcerer king, that for all their pretences they still find themselves in the position of having to rely upon the Essences of the Solars, implicitly acknowledging the supremacy of those that overthrew them.<br /> <br /> I, for one, feel as though that image of being a figure of phenomenal cosmic power that so many seemed to find attractive before fits rather nicely as the twisted counterpart to the persona of being the teacher and holy prophet. A pretty large cross section of what a lot of people found so compelling about the Green Sun Princes of yesterday, the more philosophical and transformative stuff, that seems to me like it could all go under the umbrella of Lore alone. Like, maybe some of it spills over into Integrity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T14:57:39-07:00","id":1387600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1157439-how-complicated-should-infernals-be?p=1387575#post1387575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Each Solar Ability kind of portrays its own little miniature heroic narrative. ...<br /> <br /> The developers still refer to Infernals as a twisted distortion of the Solars, and it makes me wonder if that could not work down to the level of the Abilities; take the driving character underlying each one and figure out a personality that would come across as a version that is subversive, appropriated to a more callous or self-involved nature or given particularly violent and domineering extremes. Within that structure, the aesthetics of the Yozis are merely the means of achieving that personality, rather than the personality in their own right.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes! I can definitely see that.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T15:29:21-07:00","id":1387606,"title":"","content":"I'm looking forward to seeing some of Infernal Monster Style return in Infernal Brawl. Though some of it will probably have to go to Athletics, Presence, or Resistance, especially the wild expansion Charms the fans wrote for the style.<br /> <br /> But while that means breaking up Infernal Monster Style, it means that the cruel, haughty, terrifying character of the Infernal Monster will permeate the Infernal Charmset.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T16:01:23-07:00","id":1387609,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Infernal Monster works excellently for Brawl.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T19:57:28-07:00","id":1387633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1157439-how-complicated-should-infernals-be?p=1387609#post1387609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, Infernal Monster works excellently for Brawl.</div> </div> </div> </div>Essentially, Infernal Brawl should be similar enough to Solar Brawl that it should be easy for Exalted Essence to have Generic Brawl Charms, with the &quot;Modes&quot; for Solars distinguishing them from Infernals, who are likewise distinguish by the Infernal Modes of their Charms.<br /> <br /> Like, the Solar Mode might let you hit someone one more time with the flurry-of-punches Charm, and the Infernal one might let you hit twice more if they're prone -- kicking them while they're down, as per a canonical Infernal Monster Charm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T02:32:59-07:00","id":1387669,"title":"","content":"Eh, I don't think Vance and Minton should write Infernals based on Essence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T02:51:37-07:00","id":1387674,"title":"","content":"Premise: I never played Infernals, I started with 3E and I know the still not published splats only by osmosis and the description given until now.<br /> <br /> I think -and that's only my personal preference, but I think it fits the Infernal pretty well- that at least some part of the characterization of the Infernals should be... Solar, but weird. Sorcerously weird. They are, after all, Exalted by the corruption of a Solar Exaltation by the infernal powers of the creators of the world... creators of the world that, by what I gathered, are the original owner of what's called 'Solar Sorcery'. <br /> <br /> Now, that could depend on the fact that I don't know what each Yozi represents in detail and so I can't think of specific charms for all of them, but I think that having each Charm be directly linked at one Yozi is... kind of limiting in a way. A little like how Dragon-blooded Charms are linked to a particular element and that mess up the ability of the Dragon-blooded to mix-and-match them. It would a lot more simple if the charms were neutral and then acquired specific bonus depending on the patron Yozi of the Infernal (which, incidentally, is how I would home-rule the Dragon-blooded, because I hate how Aura work for the normal charms: I like much more the approach used for the Immaculate Martial Arts).<br /> <br /> For me, the base Infernal Charms should be, in a way, sorcerous Solar Power: they accomplish -mostly- the same thing as the Solar do, but instead of being fueled by superhuman perfection, they do it in an unnatural way. Athletics Charms don't make the Infernal faster: they slow down everyone else or distort the space so he gets there first. Lore Charms don't find secret information by virtue of illuminated knowledge: they force the information out of the dark by the dictate of the Green Sun Princes. Etc etc.<br /> <br /> You could build the various varieties of the Charms depending on the Yozi after that, like there are various variety of some Dragon-blooded charms. It probably is a concept more fit for Essence that for the main splat, but I would like the Infernal put in that way: it makes them more like a variation of the Solar than... whatever they were before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25288-shapechanger","name":"Shapechanger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25288_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T04:55:55-07:00","id":1387684,"title":"","content":"Confession:<br /> <br /> I only read page 1.<br /> <br /> I think y'all are over thinking this.<br /> <br /> Solars have Charms called things like Ox Stunning Blow.<br /> <br /> If Infernals have Charms called things like Sky Twisting Strength, that doesn't have to no be an &quot;Isodios Charm&quot; anymore than the Unconquered Sun needs to have a passion for stunning oxen with his bare fists. Sky Twisting Strength can lead to Order Shattering Prana just as Ox Stunning Blow leads to Cancel the Apocalypse. There doesn't need to be a thematic link between oxen and the Apocalypse in the Solar Charmset.<br /> <br /> The Infernal Charms need to reflect the Yozi as a whole. It doesn't need to be &quot;This is the Ebon Dragon version of the Malfeas Melee Charm&quot;. It can just be &quot;This is a Melee Charm inspired by how the Yozi rend their foes&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T07:15:43-07:00","id":1387708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1157439-how-complicated-should-infernals-be?p=1387684#post1387684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Infernal Charms need to reflect the Yozi as a whole. It doesn't need to be &quot;This is the Ebon Dragon version of the Malfeas Melee Charm&quot;. It can just be &quot;This is a Melee Charm inspired by how the Yozi rend their foes&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's basically what I want, yeah. Easier and more flexible.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T07:49:34-07:00","id":1387719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1157439-how-complicated-should-infernals-be?p=1387669#post1387669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, I don't think Vance and Minton should write Infernals based on Essence.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not what I meant to suggest.<br /> <br /> I was merely suggesting that while Infernal Brawl Charms would be noticeably distinct from Solar Brawl Charms, at the end of the day, the Brawl Ability has a similar character for all Ability-based Exalted.<br /> <br /> Under the traditional model of printing entire books for each distinct splat, it makes sense to have an entirely separate Solar Brawl Charm tree and an entirely separate Infernal Brawl Charm tree.<br /> <br /> But if one wanted to simplify things, it would theoretically be possible to write a single Brawl Charm tree with each Charm having little caveats so that the Charms work a little differently for each splat.<br /> <br /> It would certainly be superior to how the Second Edition Abyssal manual tried to save on word-count by using &quot;This works just like the Solar Charm, <i>but</i>&quot; so often.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T02:24:44-07:00","id":1387958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Confession:<br /> <br /> I only read page 1.<br /> <br /> I think y'all are over thinking this.<br /> <br /> Solars have Charms called things like Ox Stunning Blow.<br /> <br /> If Infernals have Charms called things like Sky Twisting Strength, that doesn't have to no be an &quot;Isodios Charm&quot; anymore than the Unconquered Sun needs to have a passion for stunning oxen with his bare fists. Sky Twisting Strength can lead to Order Shattering Prana just as Ox Stunning Blow leads to Cancel the Apocalypse. There doesn't need to be a thematic link between oxen and the Apocalypse in the Solar Charmset.<br /> <br /> The Infernal Charms need to reflect the Yozi as a whole. It doesn't need to be &quot;This is the Ebon Dragon version of the Malfeas Melee Charm&quot;. It can just be &quot;This is a Melee Charm inspired by how the Yozi rend their foes&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given the things that you said in the last big discussion about Infernals, I'm surprised to see you taking a position such as this.<br /> <br /> Still, regardless of whether or not what you're stating here has merits, this was a topic that I began in response to some actual conversation taking place around the forum back in late 2017. It didn't just spring up out of nowhere, there was a trend and I was questioning it.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, bringing up posts or threads completely out of the community context in which they were initially made and interrogating them as though they were contemporary is generally why thread necromancy on the order of several years is such a ridiculous thing to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T04:23:47-07:00","id":1387977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1157439-how-complicated-should-infernals-be?p=1387958#post1387958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Given the things that you said in the last big discussion about Infernals, I'm surprised to see you taking a position such as this.<br /> <br /> Still, regardless of whether or not what you're stating here has merits, this was a topic that I began in response to some actual conversation taking place around the forum back in late 2017. It didn't just spring up out of nowhere, there was a trend and I was questioning it.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, bringing up posts or threads completely out of the community context in which they were initially made and interrogating them as though they were contemporary is generally why thread necromancy on the order of several years is such a ridiculous thing to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heh. I didn't notice this was such an old thread.<br /> <br /> When I came to 3E, Exalted 2E was one of my favourite RPGs. If not my absolute favourite. Any deviation from what I considered to be a (practically) perfect game, I approached with hostility. Infernals were my favourite splat, and I wanted 3E to faithfully recreate that experience.<br /> <br /> Having played 3E... it's not the same game. I can get mad that it's not the same game, or I can accept that this is a new game and enjoy it on its merits.<br /> <br /> 3E Exalted is very enjoyable on its own merits, if you are willing and able to set aside how you think it should work and instead accept how it does work. And 3E <i>does work</i> -- especially the work of the current devs. (If the new Alchemicals and Infernals are enjoyable, 3E might become my favourite RPG. It's not there yet, but with Solars, Lunars and Deebs I'm enjoying it about as much as I enjoyed 1E. I'm hopeful about Exingents.)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=08WdaNZBlGU\" target=\"_blank\">No matter what I do, 3E will be 3E. I may wish for 1E or 2E, but I will get 3E.</a><br /> <br /> Giving up the illusion that the game is wrong and I am right, and instead adopting the position that the game is probably right and I am playing wrong, has increased my enjoyment of all RPGs immensely. Especially 3E. And what I cannot accept, I change (then I share the headcanon/houserule with this good forum and move on with my life).<br /> <br /> Reframing my above post as I see the thread necromancy. Essence is going to have generic Charms the splats tweak. This works for Essence.<br /> <br /> What works for Essence is probably not appropriate for the main gameline, but the principle of Infernals having Ability based Charms inspired by <i>the</i> Yozi (collectively) seems in line with 3E design. And this is going to result in a Charmset that I imagine will have recognisable parallels with the Essence Charmset and with the Solar Charmset.<br /> <br /> But really, who knows? I wouldn't be overly upset by Yozis like DB Elements. We'll see what happens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 05-13-2020, 07:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T05:18:29-07:00","id":1387990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1157439-how-complicated-should-infernals-be?p=1387977#post1387977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What works for Essence is probably not appropriate for the main gameline, but the principle of Infernals having Ability based Charms inspired by <i>the</i> Yozi (collectively) seems in line with 3E design. And this is going to result in a Charmset that I imagine will have recognisable parallels with the Essence Charmset and with the Solar Charmset.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think of something like this and I think it would be similar to the Infernals of Burn Legend. I think that would be functional, but by this point unsatisfying to a lot of what people expect out of them. <br /> <br /> The compelling individual qualities of the Yozis are out of the bag, and barring them being found to be completely unworkable I think that some acknowledgement of them is desirable and unavoidable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But really, who knows? I wouldn't be overly upset by Yozis like DB Elements. We'll see what happens.</div> </div> </div> </div>But I think going that deep mechanically would exacerbate the issues I began this discussion with when there are so many of the Yozis, and might end up with something that pulls heavily away from the Green Sun Prince image. I think there's an effective middle ground where the Yozis are recognizable but not distinguished with Keywords.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T05:58:43-07:00","id":1387999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1157439-how-complicated-should-infernals-be?p=1387990#post1387990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think of something like this and I think it would be similar to the Infernals of Burn Legend. I think that would be functional, but by this point unsatisfying to a lot of what people expect out of them. <br /> <br /> The compelling individual qualities of the Yozis are out of the bag, and barring them being found to be completely unworkable I think that some acknowledgement of them is desirable and unavoidable.<br /> <br /> But I think going that deep mechanically would exacerbate the issues I began this discussion with when there are so many of the Yozis, and might end up with something that pulls heavily away from the Green Sun Prince image. I think there's an effective middle ground where the Yozis are recognizable but not distinguished with Keywords.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. I anticipate Charms to be things like &quot;Sky Twisting Strength&quot;, &quot;Black Boar Endurance&quot;, &quot;Creation Maiming Hoof&quot;, etc. and I expect that the names and themes of the 2E Charms will return to a greater or lesser extent. I just don't expect discrete Charm trees with Keywords etc. within Abilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T06:03:57-07:00","id":1388002,"title":"","content":"I think you can definitely have green fire, shadows, commanding lesser spirits, granting wishes for favours, etc, without having Yozi keywords or whatever, yeah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T07:02:00-07:00","id":1388033,"title":"","content":"2E Infernal charmsets seem to have been made with the intent that they should be largely self-contained and that an individual Infernal focuses on one or two with perhaps a little dabbling outside those lines. It also had each Infernal Caste tied to a specific Yozi.<br /> <br /> It seems like that's not so much going to be the case in 3E. The Ascendant Caste writeup we saw on the Discord mentioned the Yozi in collective but no singular Yozi as the Caste's patron, and combined with the plan for Ability-based Charms, I figure we're headed for Infernals who draw on the combined glory and power of the Yozi as a group overall first and foremost. I suspect we might be getting something at least vaguely akin to Lanaya's Infernal brew, in which a single Ability might draw on different Yozi for its different aspects---Adorjan is reflected in Athletics charms about speed and mobility, while Malfeas or Isidoros might be the face behind feats of strength and demolition. I think I'd like that to be the case, certainly.<br /> <br /> I also think that, a little like the stated Abyssal model, the specific Yozi nuances might be less specific at the start of the tree and get more overt as you go deeper in. Those mobility-centric Athletics Charms might start just as general expressions of hellish excellence, but then get more and more specifically reflective of Adorjan's themes as they go along.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}